cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Zetikon"
abstract: >-
  Zetikon is a theoretical framework and software application for analyzing,
  optimizing, compiling, and transforming algorithms. It is predicated on the
  notion of tripartite representation equivalence insofar that an algorithm 
  is equivalently represented as a text, system of equations, or geometry.
  The geometry is an orthotope that is equivalent to the image of the so-called
  master representation of an algorithm. The master representation of an algorithm
  is constructed by a mathematical object called a loop-vector. The framing gives 
  rise to several interesting properties such as reformulating algorithm complexity
  analysis as factorizations of the induced orthotope's volume.
type: software
authors:
